================================================================================
SCOPE — what this MIT grant does and does not cover
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the *code* in this repository: the analysis scripts,
the capture and measurement pipeline, the agent harnesses, the reproduction
drivers (`install.sh`, `artifact/REPRODUCE.sh`, `artifact/verify.py`, each
`rq*/scripts/run_repro.sh`, each `claims/*/run.sh`,
`rq*/analyze_*.py`, `rq*/plot_*.py`), the packaging files (`Dockerfile`,
`notebooks/`), and the documentation.

EXCEPTION — third-party filter lists. The files under

    pipeline/classifier/tracker_lists/

are verbatim March-2026 snapshots of filter lists maintained by third parties.
They are NOT relicensed by this file and are NOT covered by the MIT grant
above. Each snapshot remains under its own upstream license (GPL-3.0,
GPL-3.0 / CC-BY-SA-3.0 dual, and one free-for-research-with-attribution list).
The per-file license mapping, upstream URLs, and snapshot dates are recorded in

    pipeline/classifier/tracker_lists/LICENSES.md

Read that file before redistributing, modifying, or embedding any of those
snapshots. The derived lookup table `tracker_domains_7list.json` in the same
directory is generated from those snapshots and inherits their terms.

NOTE — research data. The measurement data shipped under `rq*/data/`,
`cross_benchmark/data/`, `data/`, and the Tier-2 archives are released for
research use as described in the "Data tiers" section of `README.md`. Tier-3
raw flow bodies and cookie values are not released (IRB protocol). No personal
data is included in this repository; cookie values appear only as per-campaign
salted hashes, and the salt is not released.
